SolidInvoice on FenrirOS
========================

Code in /usr/share/solidinvoice (web root: public/). config/env, where
SolidInvoice keeps its encrypted settings and their keys, is
/etc/solidinvoice; optional environment overrides go in
/etc/solidinvoice/local.env (read as .env.local); var/ (cache, logs) is
/var/lib/solidinvoice/var. PHP runs as _php. SolidInvoice needs PHP 8.4.27
or newer.

1. Database: create a MariaDB (or PostgreSQL) database and user, or use
   SQLite (the wizard's default puts it in /etc/solidinvoice/db; to keep it in
   /var/lib instead put
     SOLIDINVOICE_DATABASE_URL=sqlite:////var/lib/solidinvoice/solidinvoice.db
   in /etc/solidinvoice/local.env).
2. nginx: /usr/share/doc/solidinvoice/nginx-solidinvoice.conf (and,
   optionally, the php-fpm pool php-fpm-solidinvoice.conf); enable php-fpm
   and nginx (dinitctl enable php-fpm nginx), then open https://<host>/ and
   follow the first-run wizard (database, administrator, company). It
   writes the settings and generates this installation's keys in
   /etc/solidinvoice.
3. Background worker (mail, recurring invoices, reminders):
     cp /usr/share/doc/solidinvoice/solidinvoice.cron /etc/cron.d/solidinvoice
     dinitctl enable crond
4. Telemetry is off unless SOLIDINVOICE_ENABLE_TELEMETRY=1. The Cloud
   affiliate prompt can be hidden with SOLIDINVOICE_AFFILIATE_PROGRAM_ENABLED=0
   in local.env.
5. After an update of this package, as _php:
     /usr/share/solidinvoice/bin/console cache:clear
     /usr/share/solidinvoice/bin/console doctrine:migrations:migrate --no-interaction
